# Tutor rot drill

The tutorial's `keys` fields are executable documentation. A default binding
may move only when its lesson metadata moves in the same change.

`make test-tutor` enforces that rule with a hermetic mutation drill. The drill
copies `runtime/`, renames L mode's `i` binding to `z` in the copy, and runs
the Chapter 1 PTY replay against that copied runtime. The replay must fail at
the task-engine verdict for entering Insert mode. It then reruns the same case
against the pristine checked-in runtime and requires a green, deterministic
replay. Neither half edits the source tree or user state.

To reproduce the complete check:

```text
make test-tutor
```

When intentionally changing a binding taught by the tutor, update the
corresponding `keys` value and prose in `runtime/tutor/ch??-*.fl` and
`runtime/tutor/text/ch??.txt` in the same commit. Never weaken the drill to
accept a stale lesson.
